# Fictional EP Tracklist

## 1. Five Cuts Cross the Fourth Kick

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 160 BPM. Malik begins with a sparse footwork pattern containing four recognizable low-kick landmarks across two bars, but large gaps remain between them. Seo-jin enters with a five-attack geomungo figure: one low open string, two muted mid-string hits, one bent fourth, and one hard suldae return. Because the figure repeats continuously, its strongest fifth attack lands over a different part of the drum pattern every cycle.

Min-chae adds a clipped two-beat clavinet cell built from an open fifth and minor seventh. The cell repeats normally, making the rotating geomungo feel even less anchored. Hae-rin contributes one dry janggu stick stroke only in bars where both kick and snare leave the same subdivision empty. Andre waits until Seo-jin shifts the figure upward, then adds two short chalumeau pulses separated by a fourth.

At the midpoint, Malik removes one kick but leaves all acoustic cycles unchanged. The footwork pattern appears to tilt even though neither tempo nor geomungo phrasing changes. In the final thirty seconds, Seo-jin keeps the five-attack grouping but transfers the strongest accent from attack five to attack two. The notes remain identical; the entire groove feels rebuilt.

